  "content": {
    "id": "p21-p1-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "1",
    "prompt": "Solve the following for $\\theta\\in[0^\\circ,360^\\circ]$.",
    "layout": "grid",
    "columns": 2,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p21-p1-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$\\sin(2\\theta-60^\\circ)=1$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\theta=75^\\circ,255^\\circ$.",
          "worked": "Let $u=2\\theta-60^\\circ$. The transformed domain is $u\\in[-60^\\circ,660^\\circ]$.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\sin u&=1\\\\u&=90^\\circ,450^\\circ\\\\2\\theta-60^\\circ&=90^\\circ,450^\\circ\\\\2\\theta&=150^\\circ,510^\\circ\\\\\\theta&=75^\\circ,255^\\circ\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 39
      },
      {
        "id": "p21-p1-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$\\cos(3\\theta+45^\\circ)=-\\dfrac{1}{\\sqrt2}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\theta=30^\\circ,60^\\circ,150^\\circ,180^\\circ,270^\\circ,300^\\circ$.",
          "worked": "Let $u=3\\theta+45^\\circ$. The transformed domain is $u\\in[45^\\circ,1125^\\circ]$. The related angle is $45^\\circ$, and cosine is negative in quadrants II and III.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\cos u&=-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt2}\\\\u&=135^\\circ,225^\\circ,495^\\circ,\\\\&\\quad585^\\circ,855^\\circ,945^\\circ\\\\3\\theta+45^\\circ&=135^\\circ,225^\\circ,495^\\circ,\\\\&\\quad585^\\circ,855^\\circ,945^\\circ\\\\3\\theta&=90^\\circ,180^\\circ,450^\\circ,\\\\&\\quad540^\\circ,810^\\circ,900^\\circ\\\\\\theta&=30^\\circ,60^\\circ,150^\\circ,\\\\&\\quad180^\\circ,270^\\circ,300^\\circ\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 54
      }
    ]
  },
